There is licensed code in Tru64 that HP does not have the rights 
to give away.  LSM is licensed from Veritas, there are System V 
bits that are licensed from (either Novel or SCO depending on who 
the courts decides holds the UNIX(tm) rights), OFS/1 (the basis of 
Tru64) license is held by the X/Open group (I think), etc...

Besides, HP wants Alpha customers to migrate to HP-UX/itanium.  
Why would they encourage you to keep your current OS, and why oh 
why would they aid you in doing it without a support contract :-)

As for Tru64 code in HP-UX, we tried to get it into HP-UX, but 
they cancelled the TruClusters/AdvFS porting project, and laid off 
all the engineers, managers, doc writers, QA, IT support dudes and 
dudets working on it.

The good news is, there are a lot of companies in the Boston, 
Southern NH region that now have some very talented kernel 
developers working for them :-)

                                        Bob Harris


