In a way my post was tongue-in-cheek. It is a shame tho' My background
is Solaris and Linux, but I've only been working with Tru64 for a year
first keeping a very loaded 8200/4100 cluster with 2 racks full of
disks up
24/7/365, along with 10 others from ES40's to DS20E's. I now have to
keep
an ES40 and DS20E running with a very very light load for the next 3
years.

(that environment along with the application has been replaced with a
rack
full of pSeries/AIX boxes).

I have grown to like both the DEC Alpha hardware and some of the
features of Tru64, with the OSSC and Linux affinity kit, the
combination
has been just as stable as any of the Solaris environments I've been
involved
with, and I feel that if DEC didn't have its (fill in the non PC part)
it could
have been a killer combination.

Oh well, I think I'll keep a DS20E for myself just as a reminder of
what
can happen to a company like DEC.

-pete "yup now admin'in AIX again"

